    {
      "id": "38e963772805-q3",
      "number": 3,
      "question": "What is pro-vitamin A or the anti-cancer compound present in carrots called? &#2327;&#2366;&#2332;&#2352; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2350;&#2380;&#2332;&#2370;&#2342; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2379;-&#2357;&#2367;&#2335;&#2366;&#2350;&#2367;&#2344; &#2319; &#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2376;&#2306;&#2360;&#2352; &#2352;&#2379;&#2343;&#2368; &#2351;&#2380;&#2327;&#2367;&#2325; &#2325;&#2379; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2361;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;?",
      "questionHtml": "<span class=\"eqt\"><p>What is pro-vitamin A or the anti-cancer compound present in carrots called?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2327;&#2366;&#2332;&#2352; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2350;&#2380;&#2332;&#2370;&#2342; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2379;-&#2357;&#2367;&#2335;&#2366;&#2350;&#2367;&#2344; &#2319; &#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2376;&#2306;&#2360;&#2352; &#2352;&#2379;&#2343;&#2368; &#2351;&#2380;&#2327;&#2367;&#2325; &#2325;&#2379; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2361;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;?</p></span>",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "Beta-carotene &#2348;&#2368;&#2335;&#2366; &#2325;&#2376;&#2352;&#2379;&#2335;&#2368;&#2344;",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">Beta-carotene</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2348;&#2368;&#2335;&#2366; &#2325;&#2376;&#2352;&#2379;&#2335;&#2368;&#2344;</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "Alpha-resins &#2309;&#2354;&#2381;&#2347;&#2366;-&#2352;&#2375;&#2332;&#2367;&#2344;",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">Alpha-resins</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2309;&#2354;&#2381;&#2347;&#2366;-&#2352;&#2375;&#2332;&#2367;&#2344;</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "Delta-terpenes &#2337;&#2375;&#2354;&#2381;&#2335;&#2366;-&#2335;&#2375;&#2352;&#2346;&#2375;&#2344;&#2381;&#2360;",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">Delta-terpenes</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2337;&#2375;&#2354;&#2381;&#2335;&#2366;-&#2335;&#2375;&#2352;&#2346;&#2375;&#2344;&#2381;&#2360;</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "Alpha-terpenoid &#2309;&#2354;&#2381;&#2347;&#2366;-&#2335;&#2375;&#2352;&#2346;&#2375;&#2344;&#2379;&#2311;&#2337;",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">Alpha-terpenoid</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2309;&#2354;&#2381;&#2347;&#2366;-&#2335;&#2375;&#2352;&#2346;&#2375;&#2344;&#2379;&#2311;&#2337;</span>"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "A",
      "solution": "<p><b>Beta-carotene</b> is a prominent carotenoid pigment found in carrots and other orange, yellow, and dark green leafy vegetables and fruits. It is a pro-vitamin A, meaning the human body can convert it into vitamin A (retinol). Beta-carotene is also known for its antioxidant properties, which contribute to its potential anti-cancer effects.</p><p><b>Explanation of Other Options:</b></p><p><b>&#8226; </b>Alpha-resins: Resins are complex chemical compounds, often found in plant exudates. Alpha-resins (like humulones) are specific compounds found in hops, contributing to the bitterness of beer, not the pro-vitamin A in carrots.</p><p><b>&#8226; </b>Delta-terpenes: Terpenes are a large and diverse class of organic compounds produced by a variety of plants. While carotenoids (like beta-carotene) are tetraterpenoids, \"delta-terpenes\" is not a specific well-known pro-vitamin A compound in carrots.</p><p><b>&#8226; </b>Alpha-terpenoid: Terpenoids (or isoprenoids) are a class of naturally occurring organic chemicals derived from isoprene. Beta-carotene is a terpenoid, but \"alpha-terpenoid\" is a general classification, not the specific name of the pro-vitamin A compound in carrots.</p><p><b>Further insights:</b></p><p>&#8226; Vitamin A is essential for vision, immune function, cell growth, and reproduction.</p><p>&#8226; Carotenoids like beta-carotene, alpha-carotene, and beta-cryptoxanthin are precursors to vitamin A.</p><p>&#8226; The antioxidant properties of beta-carotene help protect cells from damage caused by free radicals, which may play a role in cancer development.</p>",
